The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its own cause table says
otherwise. Read report by report, against each reporter's tenant, the ticket holds separate
problems. Each one needs its own fix, and the parser fix queued for #4471 only reaches the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. The queued parser fix leaves the other problems below open.
</Callout>

## What the reports show

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{ parser: `${REPO}/issues/1`, hint: `${REPO}/issues/2`, 'one-day': `${REPO}/issues/3` }}
/>

## How each report was placed

1. One report per id. The ticket system exports in overlapping pages, so some reports come twice.
2. The desk's one-day notes go first. A report that says the date moved by one day did not get a
   flipped month, whatever its tenant.
3. Every other report goes by its tenant and the way it came in, as
   [`causes.ts`](https://github.com/CamiloGaete/support-kb-4471/blob/main/src/lib/kb/causes.ts) runs it: a form
   report from a day-first tenant on booking-v3 is `hint`, the rest is `parser`.
4. Intake's tag is not used. It is a guess from the reporter's browser, and the table shows how
   often it names the other cause.

Every body was read. Each report placed under `parser` or `hint` either swaps day and month, or
gives no date to check against.

## What changes for the desk

- **parser** is what #4471 already describes, and its queued fix stays the right fix for these
  reports.
- **hint** survives that fix. booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, so
  people at day-first tenants type the month first, and the form reads their input day first.
  The form needs the tenant's own order under its date field, as booking-v2 already does.
- **one-day** is a third bug: the date lands a day early or late, and one report has the same
  meeting on different days in Lisbon and Toronto. Look at how the date crosses time zones on
  its way into the invite.
- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. The subjects
  table shows why that put these problems in one ticket. A new decision record should replace
  0001; this page does not edit it.

